us-local-allentown	1988	flat	{"rate":0.01}	https://apps.dced.pa.gov/munstats-public/ReportInformation2.aspx?report=taxes_Dyn_Excel	Resident earned income tax 1% in total (city and Allentown School District 0.5% each under the Act 511 sharing rule). From the PA DCED Municipal Statistics 'Municipal Tax Information' report for reporting year 1988 (Allentown City, Lehigh County). The DCED report lists each body's stated Act 511 rate before the sharing rule halves them (municipal 1.0 + Allentown City S D 1.0 for reporting year 1988); the effective resident total is half the sum, as the city's codified ordinances (1.35% from 2011-2012, 1.975% from 2018), its budget announcements (the extra resident/nonresident levy cut from 0.35% to 0.33% for 2014; the city resident rate raised from 1.15% to about 1.5% for 2017) and ACIR's 1986-1994 tables (1.0) confirm.	f
