us-local-canton	1982	flat	{"rate":0.02}	https://codelibrary.amlegal.com/codes/canton/latest/canton_oh/0-0-0-4354	Canton Codified Ordinances § 181.14(d)-(e) (Allocation of funds; American Legal Publishing) narrates the rate history: increases from 1% to 1.3% effective September 1, 1968, to 1.4% effective January 1, 1969 and to 1.5% effective January 1, 1970 (Ord. 200-68, passed by voters 6-20-68), then from 1.5% to 1.9% effective October 1, 1981 and from 1.9% to 2% effective October 1, 1982 (Ord. 239-84, passed 12-17-84); § 181.03 levies 2.0% on and after October 1, 1982. 1.9% through September 30, 1982 and 2% from October 1, 1982; recorded at the year-end rate, as for the other Ohio cities. The Department of Taxation's LG-11 table prints 2% for 1983. The city's 2017 Popular Annual Financial Report (cantonohio.gov/ArchiveCenter/ViewFile/Item/93, p. 17) says 'City voters approved a tax increase in 1984 to 2%'; § 181.14(e) itself dates from Ord. 239-84 (December 1984) but states the October 1, 1981 and October 1, 1982 effective dates, so the 1984 vote is read as confirming the levy rather than starting it.	f
