us-local-glendale-opt	2004	fixed	{"amount":5,"minimumEarnings":750,"per":"month"}	https://web.archive.org/web/20040110184623/http://www.glendale.co.us:80/departments/administration/finances/Occupational_Tax_Return.pdf	Employee occupational privilege tax of $5 per month on employees receiving $750 or more in the month for work in Glendale (city Occupational Privilege Tax Return and instructions, Wayback capture of January 10, 2004; employers match $5). The tax was enacted by Ord. 21, Series of 2003 (secs. 3.21.010 and 3.21.030: $5 per month, employee defined by at least $750 in the calendar month), adopted December 2, 2003 after the November 2003 vote; the city's January 2000 tax page said it had no occupation or head tax, so 2004 is the first full year (hence 'since').	f
us-local-glendale-opt	2005	fixed	{"amount":5,"minimumEarnings":750,"per":"month"}	https://web.archive.org/web/20040110184512/http://www.glendale.co.us:80/departments/administration/finances/Occupational_Priv_Tax_Ordinance21.pdf	Employee occupational privilege tax of $5 per month on employees receiving at least $750 in the calendar month: Ord. 21, Series of 2003, secs. 3.21.010 and 3.21.030 (Wayback copy from the city site), as in the 2004 return; Ord. 2005-5 amended both sections, and the current code (eCode360) still gives $5 and $750. Year-specific documents not located.	f
us-local-glendale-opt	2006	fixed	{"amount":5,"minimumEarnings":750,"per":"month"}	https://ecode360.com/47868031	Glendale Municipal Code ch. 3.21 (eCode360): sec. 3.21.030 employee occupational privilege tax of $5 per month; sec. 3.21.010 defines an employee as one receiving at least $750 in the calendar month. Both sections enacted by Ord. 2003-21 and amended by Ord. 2005-5 sec. 1, with no later amendment (Ord. 2019-7 amended only sec. 3.21.050); recorded from the first full year after the 2005 ordinance. Year-specific documents not located.	f
