us-local-in-adams	1973	none	{}	https://newspapers.library.in.gov/?a=d&d=BG19730628-01.1.14	Secondary source (Banner-Graphic, Greencastle, Indiana, Associated Press report 'Deadline For Second Tax Phase Is Sunday', June 28, 1973, via Hoosier State Chronicles): the Adams County Council turned down the 1973 local option income tax. The county adjusted gross income tax, Indiana's first county income tax, was enacted in 1973; counties adopting it by June 1, 1973 imposed it from July 1, 1973 (31 counties did), and those adopting by July 1 imposed it from January 1, 1974. So no county income tax in 1973. Single secondary source.	f
