us-local-in-elkhart	1974	flat	{"deduction":{"single":1000,"marriedJoint":2000},"rate":0.01}	https://codelibrary.amlegal.com/codes/elkhartcounty/latest/elkhartco_in/0-0-0-1143	Resident rate is the combined CAGIT or COIT plus CEDIT rate for the calendar year; the components are not modelled separately. Deduction is the $1,000 per person exemption. Elkhart County Code chapter 36 adopts CAGIT at 1% for resident county taxpayers by ordinance passed May 19, 1973 (section 36.016) and CEDIT at 0.25% by Ord. CC-90-1(a), passed March 21, 1990 (section 36.030); no other county income tax enactment falls between them. The Nappanee Advance-News reports the 1% rate in effect from July 1, 1973 (November 7, 1974) and still 'the present county tax rate of one percent' in February 1990, with CEDIT revenue arriving from 1991 (February 28 and September 12, 1990). So 1% for the whole of this year.	f
