us-local-in-jackson	1973	none	{}	https://newspapers.library.in.gov/?a=d&d=BG19730628-01.1.14	Secondary source (Banner-Graphic, Greencastle, Indiana, Associated Press report 'Deadline For Second Tax Phase Is Sunday', June 28, 1973, via Hoosier State Chronicles): the Jackson County Council rejected the 1973 local option income tax for the last half of 1973 and rejected it again for 1974. The county adjusted gross income tax, Indiana's first county income tax, was enacted in 1973; counties adopting it by June 1, 1973 imposed it from July 1, 1973 (31 counties did), and those adopting by July 1 imposed it from January 1, 1974. So no county income tax in 1973. Single secondary source.	f
