us-local-in-kosciusko	1974	flat	{"deduction":{"single":1000,"marriedJoint":2000},"rate":0.005}	https://newspapers.library.in.gov/?a=d&d=TMJ19740501.1.14	Secondary source (The Mail-Journal, Milford, Indiana, 'County to receive $358,253', May 1, 1974, via Hoosier State Chronicles): Kosciusko County's county adjusted gross income tax rate is one half per cent. The same paper reports the tax took effect July 1, 1973 (July 4, 1973), that the 1977 revenue came from the one-half of one per cent tax (January 18, 1978) and that the council voted in January 1978 to rescind it effective July 1, 1978 (January 25, 1978; July 11, 1979; February 6, 1985). Single secondary source. Resident rate is the combined CAGIT or COIT plus CEDIT rate for the calendar year; the components are not modelled separately. Deduction is the $1,000 per person exemption. 0.5% for the whole of this year.	f
