us-local-in-kosciusko	1979	none	{}	https://newspapers.library.in.gov/?a=d&d=TMJ19790711.1.9	Secondary source (The Mail-Journal, Milford, Indiana, 'County to receive funds', July 11, 1979, via Hoosier State Chronicles): no Kosciusko County collections are made because the county rescinded the county adjusted gross income tax effective July 1, 1978. The same paper reports in 1982 that the county has had no local option tax since (March 3, 1982) and that the county option income tax was first imposed in 1985 (February 6, 1985; April 19, 1989). So no county income tax this year. Single secondary source.	f
