us-local-in-kosciusko	1991	flat	{"deduction":{"single":1000,"marriedJoint":2000},"rate":0.006}	https://newspapers.library.in.gov/?a=d&d=TMJ19890419.1.15	Secondary source (The Mail-Journal, Milford, Indiana, 'In 1989 - Option tax distributions will total $3,504,000', April 19, 1989, via Hoosier State Chronicles): Kosciusko County's county option income tax began in 1985 at 0.2% and rose each year; it was 0.5% in April 1989 and under the ordinance is frozen at 0.6% from 1990. the Department of Revenue's Form IT-40P booklet chart of 1992-1996 county rates (http://web.archive.org/web/20040716084947/http://www.in.gov:80/dor/taxforms/96pdfs/it-40p.pdf, page 13) prints .006 for 1992 to 1996. So 0.6% for the whole of 1991. Single secondary source for 1991. Resident rate is the combined CAGIT or COIT plus CEDIT rate for the calendar year; the components are not modelled separately. Deduction is the $1,000 per person exemption.	f
