us-local-in-lawrence	1974	flat	{"deduction":{"single":1000,"marriedJoint":2000},"rate":0.01}	https://codelibrary.amlegal.com/codes/lawrencecoin/latest/lawrenceco_in/0-0-0-1306	Resident rate is the combined CAGIT or COIT plus CEDIT rate for the calendar year; the components are not modelled separately. Deduction is the $1,000 per person exemption. Lawrence County Code section 33.01(A) adopts CAGIT at 1% for resident county taxpayers (Bill 1144, passed June 1, 1973, the last day for imposing the tax from July 1, 1973); the code's only other county income tax provision is the additional property tax relief rate of section 33.01(B), and the Department of Revenue's Form IT-40P booklet chart of 1992-1996 county rates (http://web.archive.org/web/20040716084947/http://www.in.gov:80/dor/taxforms/96pdfs/it-40p.pdf, page 13) prints .01 for 1992 to 1996 (the county's rate first changes in 2009). So 1% for the whole of this year.	f
