us-local-in-putnam	1987	flat	{"deduction":{"single":1000,"marriedJoint":2000},"rate":0.01}	https://newspapers.library.in.gov/?a=d&d=BG19860712.1.1	Secondary source (Banner-Graphic, Greencastle, Indiana, 'CAGIT shrinks netpay', July 12, 1986, via Hoosier State Chronicles): the Putnam County Council imposed the county adjusted gross income tax at a full one percent for residents, effective July 1, 1986; the paper calls it 'a local option income tax started just this year' (September 9, 1986). On March 31, 1990 it again describes CAGIT as 'established at a rate of one percent' while the council delayed a CEDIT; the CEDIT was not adopted until February 1992 (February 14, 1992). the Department of Revenue's Form IT-40P booklet chart of 1992-1996 county rates (http://web.archive.org/web/20040716084947/http://www.in.gov:80/dor/taxforms/96pdfs/it-40p.pdf, page 13) prints .01 for 1992. So 1% for the whole of this year. Single secondary source. Resident rate is the combined CAGIT or COIT plus CEDIT rate for the calendar year; the components are not modelled separately. Deduction is the $1,000 per person exemption.	f
