us-local-in-spencer	1991	flat	{"deduction":{"single":1000,"marriedJoint":2000},"rate":0.005}	https://codelibrary.amlegal.com/codes/spencercountyin/latest/spencercounty_in/0-0-0-1390	Resident rate is the combined CAGIT or COIT plus CEDIT rate for the calendar year; the components are not modelled separately. Deduction is the $1,000 per person exemption. Spencer County Code section 36.06 imposes CEDIT at 0.5% effective July 1, 1990 (Council Ord. 1990-2, passed February 20, 1990); the county option income tax of section 36.02 is a later tax (frozen at its 2003 rate of 0.3%). the Department of Revenue's Form IT-40P booklet chart of 1992-1996 county rates (http://web.archive.org/web/20040716084947/http://www.in.gov:80/dor/taxforms/96pdfs/it-40p.pdf, page 13) prints .005 for 1992 to 1996, i.e. the CEDIT alone. So 0.5% for the whole of 1991.	f
