us-local-in-white	1974	flat	{"deduction":{"single":1000,"marriedJoint":2000},"rate":0.01}	https://codelibrary.amlegal.com/codes/whitecountyin/latest/whiteco_in/0-0-0-1033	Resident rate is the combined CAGIT or COIT plus CEDIT rate for the calendar year; the components are not modelled separately. Deduction is the $1,000 per person exemption. White County Code of Ordinances section 31.12 adopts CAGIT at 1% for resident county taxpayers (Ord. 10-73, passed May 29, 1973); the code records no later CAGIT ordinance. the Department of Revenue's Form IT-40P booklet chart of 1992-1996 county rates (http://web.archive.org/web/20040716084947/http://www.in.gov:80/dor/taxforms/96pdfs/it-40p.pdf, page 13) prints .01125 for 1993 and .0125 for 1994, i.e. a 0.25% CEDIT added on July 1, 1993. So the 1% CAGIT alone applied for the whole of this year.	f
