us-local-pittsburgh	1977	flat	{"rate":0.02}	https://books.google.com/books?id=LCYcAAAAIBAJ&pg=PA24&article_id=3422,3973576	Secondary source (The Pittsburgh Press, reader-service column 'Wage Tax Paid At Home Or Work', August 26, 1977, p. 24, via Google News Archive): the City of Pittsburgh levies a one per cent wage tax, and city residents also pay a one per cent wage tax to the school district. Resident earned income tax: city 1% + Pittsburgh School District 1% (as ACIR prints for July 1, 1976; the city rose to 1.25% from January 1979). Single secondary source.	f
