us-local-toledo	1995	flat	{"rate":0.0225}	https://cdn.toledo.oh.gov/uploads/documents/Finance/2014-Annual-Information-Statement.pdf	The City of Toledo 2014 Annual Information Statement (p. 44) states that the electors authorized an increase of the tax rate to 1-1/2% in 1966, 'in effect for a continuing period of time', and 'In 1982, the City's electors authorized a further increase of the income tax rate from 1-1/2% to 2-1/4% for a period of four years (from July 1, 1982 through June 30, 1986), which authorization has been extended through December 31, 2016 by votes of the electors of the City in 1985, 1989, 1993, 1997, 2002, 2005, 2008 and 2012.' So 2.25% applied from July 1, 1982 through 2016 (rate in effect at December 31, 1995); the ACIR Significant Features of Fiscal Federalism editions print 2.25% for 1983-1994 and the Department of Taxation's LG-11 table 2.25% for 2000. No document for 1995 itself.	f
