us-local-youngstown	1972	flat	{"rate":0.015}	https://codelibrary.amlegal.com/codes/youngstown/latest/youngstown_oh/0-0-0-6792	Youngstown Codified Ordinances § 181.04 (Effective period and purposes; American Legal Publishing) narrates the rate history as 'the one and one-half percent (1 1/2%) ... representing the prior imposed income tax', 'the remaining tax increase of one-half percent (1/2%) ... over and above the current income tax of one and one-half percent', 'the remaining tax increase of one-quarter of one percent (1/4%) ... over and above the current income tax of two percent (2%)' and 'the remaining tax increase of one-half of one percent ... over and above the current income tax of two and one-quarter percent (2 1/4%)' (the last approved by voters 11-5-02, levied from January 1, 2003 per § 181.03); § 181.01 cites Ord. 81-342 approved by voters 9-8-81. So 1.5% was the rate from before 1970 until the first increase, voted September 8, 1981; the ACIR editions print 1.5% at December 31, 1970 and 1971, July 1, 1973, July 1, 1976 and October 1, 1979. No document for 1972 itself. The 2% rate took effect September 15, 1981 (see 1981).	f
