us-local-youngstown	1981	flat	{"rate":0.02}	https://news.google.com/newspapers?nid=pqgf-8x9CmQC&dat=19810909&id=s6xJAAAAIBAJ&sjid=X4QMAAAAIBAJ&pg=768,2247846	Secondary source (Youngstown Vindicator, 'Victory Margin 2 1/2 to 1', front page, and 'City Income Tax Boost Passed; Will Take Effect Next Tuesday', p. 6, September 9, 1981, via Google News Archive): the one-half percent increase passed by voters on September 8, 1981 brings the total city income tax to 2 percent, up from 1 1/2 percent; the city would start collecting it the following Tuesday (September 15, 1981) once the Mahoning County Board of Elections certified the vote. Year-end rate recorded: 1.5% applied before mid-September 1981. Single secondary source; consistent with Codified Ordinances sec. 181.01 (Ord. 81-342, approved by voters 9-8-81) and ACIR's 2.0% for 1983.	f
