us-state-CA	1978	brackets	{"deduction":{"single":1000,"marriedJoint":2000},"schedules":{"single":[{"from":0,"rate":0.01},{"from":2100,"rate":0.02},{"from":3680,"rate":0.03},{"from":5260,"rate":0.04},{"from":6840,"rate":0.05},{"from":8420,"rate":0.06},{"from":10000,"rate":0.07},{"from":11570,"rate":0.08},{"from":13150,"rate":0.09},{"from":14730,"rate":0.1},{"from":16310,"rate":0.11}],"marriedJoint":[{"from":0,"rate":0.01},{"from":4200,"rate":0.02},{"from":7360,"rate":0.03},{"from":10520,"rate":0.04},{"from":13680,"rate":0.05},{"from":16840,"rate":0.06},{"from":20000,"rate":0.07},{"from":23140,"rate":0.08},{"from":26300,"rate":0.09},{"from":29460,"rate":0.1},{"from":32620,"rate":0.11}]}}	https://archive.org/details/micro_IA40706916_0013	Computed from the statute's indexing (Stats. 1978, ch. 569) as the California Franchise Tax Board's annual reports describe it (microfilm scans on archive.org): the 1977 schedule (FTB Table 1B; joint brackets twice the single ones, income splitting) with every bracket widened each year by that year's index factor, 5.222% for 1978, 6.88% for 1979, 17.33% for 1980, 8.26% for 1981 and 9.32% for 1982 (FTB 1982 Annual Report, Table 1A footnote 7; the 1982 factor from the 1983 Annual Report, micro_IA40706918_0345), and rounded to the nearest $10 each year. The standard deduction was indexed from 1979 by the full June-to-June California CPI change (the bracket factor plus the 3% threshold removed: 9.88% for 1979; FTB 1980 and 1981 reports), also rounded to $10. Checks against amounts the reports print: the top (11%) joint bracket starts at $44,280 for 1981 (FTB 1982 report, 'Indexing') and $48,400 for 1982 (1983 report); the joint standard deduction is $2,800 for 1981 (1982 report) and $1,530 single / $3,060 joint for 1982 (1983 report, 'Deductions'); every computed value matches. The lower brackets weren't printed for these years, so they rest on the same indexing rule. Personal and dependent exemption credits (indexed too; quadrupled one time for 1978) are tax credits, not modelled.	f
