us-state-MT	1981	brackets	{"deduction":{"single":880,"marriedJoint":1760},"schedules":{"single":[{"from":0,"rate":0.02},{"from":1100,"rate":0.03},{"from":2200,"rate":0.04},{"from":4400,"rate":0.05},{"from":6600,"rate":0.06},{"from":8800,"rate":0.07},{"from":11000,"rate":0.08},{"from":15300,"rate":0.09},{"from":21900,"rate":0.1},{"from":38400,"rate":0.11}]}}	https://mca.legmt.gov/bills/1997/mca/15/30/15-30-103.htm	Indexed schedule for tax year 1981. Computed from the statute: 15-30-103(2) MCA has the Department of Revenue multiply the base brackets of 15-30-103(1) ($1,000, $2,000, $4,000, $6,000, $8,000, $10,000, $14,000, $20,000, $35,000; rates 2%-11%) by the inflation factor for the taxable year and round the cumulative brackets to the nearest $100; 15-30-112(6) does the same for the $800 personal exemption, rounded to the nearest $10; 15-30-101(8) defines the inflation factor as the consumer price index for June of the taxable year divided by the CPI for June 1980 (MCA 1997 text, mca.legmt.gov; indexing enacted by Initiative 86, approved November 4, 1980, and 15-30-103 not amended again until Ch. 634, L. 1993). CPI-U, U.S. city average, all items, 1967=100, not seasonally adjusted (BLS series CUUR0000AA0): June 1980 247.6. Check against published years: the same computation reproduces every bracket and the exemption printed for 1982 and 1984 (Montana Taxpayers Digest), 1986, 1988, 1990 (ACIR) and 1991-1992; for 1983 it gives $16,900, $24,100 and $42,100 for the top three brackets where the 1983 entry has $16,800, $24,000 and $42,000 (a factor of 1.20 rather than 1.204), and the 1987 Digest reprints the 1984 brackets. June 1981 CPI 271.3, inflation factor 1.0957: brackets $1,100, $2,200, $4,400, $6,600, $8,800, $11,000, $15,300, $21,900, $38,400; exemption $880. No surtax: the 10% surtax was repealed for taxable years after 1980 (Ch. 422, L. 1981; see this file's 1980 entry). 1981 is the first indexed year; the Montana Taxpayers Digest 1981 states that indexing starts with tax year 1981 but prints only the 1980 base schedule. Single rate table for all filing statuses (married couples filing jointly use the same table on combined income; most file separately on the same form), so no joint schedule. Deduction = personal exemptions only (1 single / 2 MFJ); Montana standard deduction is a percentage of AGI with min/max, not recorded. Deduction for federal income tax paid (itemizers) not modelled.	f
