us-state-SC	1970	brackets	{"deduction":{"single":800,"marriedJoint":1600},"schedules":{"single":[{"from":0,"rate":0.02},{"from":2000,"rate":0.03},{"from":4000,"rate":0.04},{"from":6000,"rate":0.05},{"from":8000,"rate":0.06},{"from":10000,"rate":0.07}]}}	https://library.unt.edu/gpo/acir/Reports/information/M-57.pdf	ACIR Significant Features of Fiscal Federalism 1970-71 ed. (M-57), Table 36 (State Individual Income Taxes: Rates, December 31, 1970; PDF p. 91), Table 37 (personal exemptions, December 31, 1970; p. 97) and Table 38 (standard deduction and optional tax table, December 31, 1970; p. 99); the table describes the law in force at the end of tax year 1970. 2%-7% on $2,000 steps of net income after personal exemption; same brackets for all filing statuses; the same schedule is printed in the 1969 edition (December 31, 1969) and in the 1976 edition (July 1, 1976). Federal income tax deductible, limited to $500 per taxpayer (not modelled). Deduction = $800 single / $1,600 married personal exemption; standard deduction 10% of income, max $500 single / $1,000 joint (not recorded). Exemption for persons 65+ with low income not modelled.	f
