us-state-SC	2018	brackets	{"deduction":{"single":12000,"marriedJoint":24000},"schedules":{"single":[{"from":0,"rate":0},{"from":2970,"rate":0.03},{"from":5940,"rate":0.04},{"from":8910,"rate":0.05},{"from":11880,"rate":0.06},{"from":14860,"rate":0.07}]}}	https://files.taxfoundation.org/20180926170326/State-Individual-Income-Tax-Rates1.xlsx	Secondary source (Tax Foundation, State Individual Income Tax Rates and Brackets for 2018, Fiscal Fact No. 576 data workbook, '2018' sheet): South Carolina single and joint schedules print 3% > $2,970, 4% > $5,940, 5% > $8,910, 6% > $11,880, 7% > $14,860 (income below $2,970 untaxed, the 0% bracket of S.C. Code 12-6-515). Single source; checked against the 2018 SC1040 booklet (https://taxsim.nber.org/historical_state_tax_forms/SC/2018/IITPacket_2018.pdf): rate schedule 7% minus $505 matches, and these brackets reproduce every row of its tax table (9 rows where the exact tax ends in 50 cents are printed rounded down). Starts from federal taxable income: deduction = federal standard deduction (no federal personal exemption after 2017). Same brackets for all filing statuses. SC dependent exemption, two-wage-earner credit and other SC deductions not modelled.	f
us-state-SC	2019	brackets	{"deduction":{"single":12200,"marriedJoint":24400},"schedules":{"single":[{"from":0,"rate":0},{"from":3030,"rate":0.03},{"from":6060,"rate":0.04},{"from":9090,"rate":0.05},{"from":12120,"rate":0.06},{"from":15160,"rate":0.07}]}}	https://dor.sc.gov/forms-site/Forms/SC4972_2019.pdf	SC Department of Revenue Form SC4972 (Tax on Lump-Sum Distributions), 2019, '2019 South Carolina Tax Rate Schedule': $0 below $3,030; 3% of the amount less $91 from $3,030; 4% less $152 from $6,060; 5% less $242 from $9,090; 6% less $364 from $12,120; 7% less $515 from $15,160. The constants are consistent with these bracket edges (each equals the tax at the edge under the lower rate, to the dollar). Same brackets for all filing statuses. Starts from federal taxable income: deduction = the 2019 federal standard deduction ($12,200 single, $24,400 joint), as in this file's 2018 and 2020 entries. SC dependent exemption and other SC deductions not modelled.	f
